  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rehab of Hale Hydropower - Rehab of Hale Hydropower NS</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Upprustning Hale vattenkr</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of the project is to provide renewable energy for poverty reduction. The specific objective is to ensure another 30-40 years power supply from the Hale hydropower station to the national grid, which includes improved overall operational and safety aspects of the hydropower plant. Hale power station is owned and operated by the national utility company Tanzania Electric Supply Company, Tanesco.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rehabilitation of Hale Hydro Power Plant in Tanga Region in Tanzania  encompassing replacement of one generating unit (10,5 MW), partial    renovation of the second unit plus comprehensive rehabilitation of    civil, hydraulic and electromechanical equipment and the winding of   Songo songo substation</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Upprustning av Hale vattenkraftstation i Tanga region i Tanzania inkl byte av en generator (10,5 MW), delvis renovering av den andra        generatorn, samt upprustning av utrustning och songo songo            transformatorcentralen.</narrative>
  </description>
